th_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`sensei-top report` now labels rows that have no deck as `(no deck)`, so it no longer crashes on an MTGO match with no `deck_id`. `uv run pytest -q tests/test_cli_report.py` (2 tests) and `uv run ruff check .` both pass.\n\nThe implementer's only change is in `cmd_report` in `src/sensei_top/cli.py`. It added `'(no deck)'` as the last argument of the four `COALESCE` calls: deck win-rate, play/draw, game length and per-turn averages. I read the diff and it touches nothing else. The win-rate query uses `deck_name` rather than the spec's `name`, and the implementer kept that.\n\nI didn't run the full test suite, the dashboard checks, or `report` against a real database. The spec only asked for the two commands above.", "ttft_ms": 1678, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 4595, "uuid": "98830001-94c3-458c-afbb-118251f48287", "ttft_stream_ms": 984, "time_to_request_ms": 13, "first_content_frame_ms": 984, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
